#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe8b9ab2-e01a-5b59-93c4-4bb629b755bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "336\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282925} {:answer/id #uuid "be068561-3b93-58f9-a599-4f8d05798c25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "324\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282926} {:answer/id #uuid "7e554324-d412-58e4-9b70-5dff1e735b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "354\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282927} {:answer/id #uuid "c738d2b8-ba7f-5c99-8724-113ff5888206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "348\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282928} {:answer/id #uuid "1ebb305a-5310-5baf-b0cf-78711d9eb5ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "316\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be068561-3b93-58f9-a599-4f8d05798c25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "324\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282926} :answer-field/id #uuid "a28095ac-adf3-50ac-b7cb-8f1aa95fde21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c2645ff-704d-5d0e-a816-127a2f8fd501" :question/math-academy-id "q-120078" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/8b618c8e43dbe898a6e1c481f4f887a50bc2e8c658368876be11ec5ea269a50c.png)\n\nA company produces a chocolate bar that comes in an triangular-prism-shaped box. In the figure, the areas of some of the faces are displayed in a net of the prism. What is the total surface area of the box?" :question/worked-solution "The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (central and side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the side faces}) \\\\  & +1\\times (\\text{Area of the central face}) \\\\  & =2\\times 36+2\\times 72+108 \\\\  & =72+144+108 \\\\  & =324\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3916a7c-e231-5f13-bf5c-cacbbbe98ac7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,280\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282932} {:answer/id #uuid "cdde5fdf-534d-5e22-a091-af8e8619b61c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,070\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282933} {:answer/id #uuid "0a815c2f-4fb2-5ca0-8b25-3b0628a86930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282934} {:answer/id #uuid "b06d9ab2-63b9-5b32-9328-a36c21399110" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,460\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282935} {:answer/id #uuid "addaa780-8ea2-511a-8154-9c95664852bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,160\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a815c2f-4fb2-5ca0-8b25-3b0628a86930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282934} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b661837-27bb-5ece-a120-0ddf7f7452d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "592068ce-9ec8-5687-8e1b-6c2f6c750355" :question/math-academy-id "q-120095" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/a7f100b99cdd9ff4f19209be8df1ae01d4cf1254d67f985cd6de41aefbf51e31.png)\n\nJill unfolds a cardboard box and obtains a net shown above. What is the total surface area of the box?" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a rectangular prism. The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ squares (base and top) and $4$ rectangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =2\\times 360+4\\times 420 \\\\  & =720+1\\,680 \\\\  & =2\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given Some Lengths"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5715275-9443-584a-9f88-4595cb23c2b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282939} {:answer/id #uuid "b5038f42-936a-55b9-9549-abcb1dbbb0d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282940} {:answer/id #uuid "37bcb9ba-da2d-52d7-a0a7-fd46fe972871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282941} {:answer/id #uuid "33c4ed64-44dc-52e9-992a-359432c2db69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282942} {:answer/id #uuid "d371b68b-a06f-5b1b-ad6c-f8c89e0a9a57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5038f42-936a-55b9-9549-abcb1dbbb0d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282940} :answer-field/id #uuid "5edf2a96-b1f8-5813-bf8d-903850556da7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c5c0ab9-8ba3-5d4c-b7d4-04c7169ce9d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-61903" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/0c4cf0ae740f876576ff140f488432dbfae9d26eb5e68e9bafbcc9b5a5bb286b.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular prism above if it is $4\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $3\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's consider the net of our plank.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/98eb9b74a15ad1cad75974496a370fb9b9b28f7ff57bc319500fcd31492216d3.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $4\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=4\\times 3=12\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $3\\,\\text{cm}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=3\\times 3=9\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the rectangular prism consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 12+2\\times 9 \\\\  & =48+18 \\\\  & =66\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given Some Lengths"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59fe7ec3-2b47-51f2-a6d8-0c3dcdcb1794" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282946} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e0ad09-0633-56c9-a225-c9c6e3681feb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282947} {:answer/id #uuid "d7e29223-908c-5732-a7f1-e1510d25ddc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282948} {:answer/id #uuid "17932408-ff9e-5e0f-87bc-14752939ad75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282949} {:answer/id #uuid "e6065e69-d160-59be-a092-22c12f46b879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17932408-ff9e-5e0f-87bc-14752939ad75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282949} :answer-field/id #uuid "3512f341-753f-57c9-b2bb-c7a6c4172580" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282945}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17e99f21-4a32-5f31-9b6f-4f7bf7f5a533" :question/math-academy-id "q-62107" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/248ccfcbb3de8ab63622cfaf4c823ae1c1734742f5f8c9f14b1dfae0ff79eed2.png)\n\nWhat is the surface area of the box shown above knowing that  it is $4\\,\\text{m}$ long, $1\\,\\text{m}$ wide, and $1\\,\\text{m}$ tall?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's consider the net of our box.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/c35bb0f7b049baa569a06532b516436afaf310e28870cfbd4790467d36e54809.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $4\\,\\text{m}$ long and $1\\,\\text{m}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=4\\times 1=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $1\\,\\text{m}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=1\\times 1=1\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the box consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 4+2\\times 1 \\\\  & =16+2 \\\\  & =18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a78474d8-faff-5377-8744-aa009fc440d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282953} {:answer/id #uuid "9bc4a283-631b-542b-a40a-8549e8af4be5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282954} {:answer/id #uuid "0bac7c75-2ff4-57e9-bf96-c76c797c56de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282955} {:answer/id #uuid "8e84c650-79aa-5dcc-84a5-436aaf55157c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282956} {:answer/id #uuid "8521792f-d538-5df8-8a2a-d51bcf60cb83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8521792f-d538-5df8-8a2a-d51bcf60cb83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282957} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e4d2e37-fa03-57d9-bc52-91125e82bd7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a74df61c-37fc-529e-af44-1edb9c8a16fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-93344" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/76e1fb6d652758a0e20877d7cacbd1172a0073d2ada557d1761ab6e59aab06d9.png)\n\nA gardening company is making metal spikes from the net shown above. What is the total surface area of the spike?" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a rectangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 12+4\\times 6 \\\\  & =12+24 \\\\  & =36\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
